```suggestion
                swap_scratch: if item_layout.size() == 0 {
                    UnsafeCell::new(NonNull::dangling()),
                } else {
                    blob_vec.swap_scratch =
                        UnsafeCell::new(NonNull::new(std::alloc::alloc(item_layout)).unwrap());
                }
```
Just in case there is a panic before `blob_vec.swap_scratch` is set this would prevent trying to deallocate a dangling pointer in the `BlobVec` drop impl. I don't think a panic is possible in between, but better safe than sorry.
